#include "OloEnginePCH.h"

// OLO_TEST_LAYER: L8
// =============================================================================
// DogShowcaseEvidenceTest -- issue #1533, the furred dog showcase.
//
// An original scruffy golden-retriever-type mutt (SandboxProject/Assets/Models/
// Dog, generated by build_dog.py) wearing a strand coat grown here, region by
// region, on its own bind-pose surface: short on the face, muzzle and paws; long
// feathering on the ears, chest ruff, belly and the backs of the legs; a plume on
// the tail; an undercoat under guard hair, clumped, with curl and wave (coat
// authoring v4). The eyes are their own entities riding the eye bones
// (BoneAttachmentComponent), shaded through SkinOcularSurface; the nose, lips,
// gums and tongue take their skin profiles through MaterialOverridesComponent.
//
// Evidence PNGs: OloEditor/assets/tests/visual/DogShowcase*_GL_<Path>[_*].png.
// GL only; the Vulkan cells are live captures (docs/guides/groom-animals.md).
//
// "Pixar-level cute" is the user's call, not a metric's (#1533 F3). What a frame
// cannot fake is asserted: the coat covers the dog from every hero angle, each
// layer of the look is load-bearing (fur, self-shadow, scene shadow), the coat
// stays on the body through every clip, and the cooked assets round-trip.
//
// WHICH FRAMES MEASURE WHAT (the fixture's "How each helper moves the scene"):
// a claim about motion -- shimmer in a walk, the coat through a clip, secondary
// motion -- is measured on RUNTIME frames, the guide solver stepping as in
// Play; a claim about one state -- a pair, a still, the LOD at a distance -- on
// HELD frames, the scene paused and the renderer started from the same place.
// Editor-preview frames, where the solver does not step, are only stills of a
// paused pose.
//
// RUN IT IN RELEASE: the coat is ~150k strands.
// =============================================================================

